title: "Atoma"
abstract: >-
  Atoma is a verification toolchain for Zig at the Idris2 ABI seam. It takes the
  contract a repository already declares in Idris2 and the contract its Zig
  export fn already documents, canonicalises both into one hash-checked Core
  Spec IR, checks the implementation against a deliberately small verifiable
  subset of Zig, and derives SMT verification conditions from the result. The
  shape is Ada/SPARK or Rust/Creusot: one name for the subset, the contracts and
  the toolchain. Witnesses are intended to be exported as canonical Dedukti and
  rechecked by coqchk and lean4checker before any claim is promoted from
  INCOMPLETE (Warrant) to COMPLETE (Receipt). Status: Phase 0/1 - the seam,
  layout, subset and VC gates run and the soundness theorem typechecks for a
  store-free core fragment; the kernel chain is specified, not yet run.
version: "0.1.0"
